From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:48:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: close a stopped stream before
 preparing again

q6asm_dai_prepare() only tears down the previous DSP stream when it is
RUNNING. A trigger STOP leaves it STOPPED but still open in the DSP, so
the next prepare (PipeWire stops and re-prepares streams on suspend,
xrun recovery and reconfiguration) opens it a second time:

  q6asm-dai ...: cmd = 0x10db4 returned error = 0x9
  q6asm-dai ...: DSP returned error[9]
  q6asm-dai ...: q6asm_dai_prepare: q6asm_open_write failed

The error path then frees the audio client, and every later prepare
fails with "private data null or audio client freed" until the PCM is
closed. Close the stream whenever it is not IDLE, like q6asm_dai_close()
does.

Also reset queue_ptr: snd_pcm_prepare() rewinds appl_ptr, and the stale
queue_ptr made the unsigned (appl_ptr - queue_ptr) in q6asm_dai_ack()
wrap around after a re-prepare.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096) with PipeWire: repeated
play/record cycles, node suspend/resume and WirePlumber restarts without
DSP errors.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 709b4f331..837645eee 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -224,15 +224,20 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 
 	prtd->pcm_count = snd_pcm_lib_period_bytes(substream);
-	/* rate and channels are sent to audio driver */
-	if (prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING) {
+	prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
+	/*
+	 * A stream that was stopped is still open in the DSP: close it before
+	 * opening it again, or the open fails with ADSP_EALREADY and the error
+	 * path frees the audio client, breaking every later prepare.
+	 */
+	if (prtd->state != Q6ASM_STREAM_IDLE) {
 		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
 		q6asm_cmd(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id, CMD_CLOSE);
 		q6asm_unmap_memory_regions(substream->stream,
 					   prtd->audio_client);
 		q6routing_stream_close(soc_prtd->dai_link->id,
 					 substream->stream);
-		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_STOPPED;
+		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_IDLE;
 	}
 
 	ret = q6asm_map_memory_regions(substream->stream, prtd->audio_client,
